      "text": "(A.1) d(k) = f(k + 1) − qf(k) = −ln ξk+1 ξkq . Then lim k→∞ d(k) = −lnQq := d, so that {d(k)} is bounded; i.e., there exists M > 0 with |d(k)| ≤ M. Unrolling the recurrence f(k + 1) = qf(k) + d(k) yields f(k) = q k−1f(1) + k−1 j=1 q k−1−jd(j). Dividing by qk, we have f(k) qk = f(1) q + k−1 j=1 d(j) q j+1 . Since the tail of the series is bounded by ∞ j=k |d(j)| q j+1 ≤ M ∞ j=k 1 q j+1 , the limit",
